```typescript
// Before:
if (next?.type === "text" && ID_CONTINUE.test(next.value[0])) {

// After:
if (next?.type === "text" && ID_CONTINUE.test(String.fromCodePoint(next.value.codePointAt(0)))) {
```

The issue was that `next.value[0]` on a string starting with an astral character (code point > 0xFFFF) returns a lone UTF-16 surrogate half, not the full code point. The `ID_CONTINUE` regex uses the `/u` flag and expects a full code point, so it wasn't matching astral ID_Continue characters.

The fix uses `String.fromCodePoint(next.value.codePointAt(0))` which properly extracts the first code point from the string, regardless of whether it's in the BMP or is an astral character.

